From: FineWine
Subject: [PATCH] winemac: Full-screen windows the way Mac games have them; Metal HUD toggle.

Full screen. A Windows program goes full screen by making a borderless window the size of the
screen. Wine raises such a window above the menu bar and the Dock, which keeps the menu bar
from appearing and makes the program feel unlike a Mac app. FINEWINE_FULLSCREEN picks how such
a window is presented instead:

- "space": the window is given a full-screen Space of its own, as a Mac game's window is. The
  menu bar appears when the pointer reaches the top edge (unless the program has captured the
  pointer), swiping goes back to the desktop, notifications are shown over it, and Mission
  Control shows it as an app. It leaves the Space when the program makes it smaller than the
  screen again, and stays out if the user takes it out. One window per program.
- "borderless": the window stays an ordinary window; the menu bar and the Dock hide and come
  back at the screen's edges.
- unset or "exclusive": Wine's behaviour, unchanged.

Metal HUD. A View menu with Show/Hide Metal HUD, and Option-F12 for the same. Metal only has
its overlay in a process started with MTL_HUD_ENABLED=1; each Metal layer's
developerHUDProperties then decide whether it is drawn. FINEWINE_METAL_HUD says whether it
starts shown or hidden. Without MTL_HUD_ENABLED the menu item is disabled.

